This tree was produced by tools/public-export from a single commit of a private repository.

tools/corpus_check.py looks for this file. When it is present, a document stamp that names a commit which
this repository cannot resolve (the commit exists only in the private repository) is checked for structure
only, instead of failing every run. A stamp whose commit does resolve here is still compared against that
commit, so drift in this repository's own history is still caught.

Do not copy this file into the private repository: it would switch that comparison off where history exists.
